---
description: Rules for the Hide Slack Icon GNOME extension
alwaysApply: true
---

Read `CLAUDE.md` and `PRD_Hide_Slack_Icon.md` before changing the extension.

- Hide only indicators whose id/class/name contains `slack` (case-insensitive) in `Main.panel.statusArea`.
- Remove the `GLib.timeout_add_seconds` source in `disable()` and call `.show()` on hidden actors.
- GNOME 42 (this host) uses `extension.js` + `imports`. GNOME 45+ uses `extension-esm.js`. Keep `lib/hideSlackCore.js` and `lib/hideSlackCore.esm.js` aligned.
- Install with `make install`; GNOME does not load the engineering directory directly.
